# Edge case [D7, G8, M]: edge between x and y at top level before group g declares y (y is first used outside, then declared inside the group). Membership is first-group-wins; checks zone content and that the early edge still routes correctly. Warns implicit-node on x (intended).
dir DOWN
x -> y : early
group g "G" :blue {
  y[Y]
  z[Z]
}
y -> z
